Commit:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Wed Aug 19 23:59:37 2026 -0500

    perf(engine): gate the combined-read rowid sort on Arrival, not alias count
    
    _fetch_combined_rows sorted a single store's rows by rowid unconditionally.
    A single store may DECLARE ByKey(K), and totalize then sorts on (K, id) —
    id is unique, so the key is total and the discarded rowid order could never
    have reached the output. The work was pure waste on that path.
    
    Gating on `isinstance(ordering, Arrival)` also dissolves the alias-count
    proxy: Arrival is reachable only single-store (resolve_ordering refuses it
    on an aggregate), so the ordering IS the condition the count stood in for.
    
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JpCUT3bF3dukDk5xjDejRM

