    docs(atoms): close the two totalize docstring gaps, with pins
    
    Two ruled behaviors lived only in the gate report:
    
    - int-vs-float refusal was covered only by the generic "mixed types"
      sentence. It is the interesting case precisely because Python WOULD order
      1 against 2.0 — the check is type identity, not comparability, and the
      docstring now says so and why.
    - a record carrying K but no id raises the accessor's own KeyError,
      unwrapped. OrderingError means "this ordering does not fit this data"; a
      record with no id is a broken record, a different failure.
    
    Both get a test rather than prose alone (ratchet test), including the
    boundary that a record missing K never reaches the id accessor.
    
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JpCUT3bF3dukDk5xjDejRM

