Commit:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Thu Aug 20 00:02:10 2026 -0500

    fix(atoms): OrderingError no longer blames K for an id-side refusal
    
    The sort key is (K(record), id). When equal K falls through to the id
    tie-break and THOSE do not compare, the message said "key values under
    declared key 'ts' do not compare" — pointing at impeccable key values and
    sending a reader to audit the wrong field.
    
    The message now names the records and the tuple, so it is true whichever
    element failed. Scope-the-claim: the refusal knows a location (this key's
    projection), not which element, so it says only what it knows.
    
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JpCUT3bF3dukDk5xjDejRM

