    fix(engine): ordered() adopts the envelope/payload key family rule
    
    ByKey('ts') returned [] from StoreReader.ordered while _combined_read and
    the conformance vectors (SPEC §9) resolve ts/id from the record envelope —
    one declaration, two projections depending on the surface asked (readiness
    finding F1).
    
    The rule is now one function, atoms.resolve_key_field: ts and id from the
    envelope, every other key from the flat payload, and a payload field named
    ts or id never shadows the envelope. ordered(), the lens vector generator
    and the conformance runner all bind it instead of restating it; the frozen
    lens vectors regenerate byte-identical.
    
    The prior "stored columns are not key candidates" ruling narrows rather than
    falls: kind/observer/origin are still payload-resolved on this surface, so
    their projection is empty by non-membership.
    
