Commit:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Thu Aug 20 00:35:54 2026 -0500

    fix(engine): combined read stops treating every column as a key candidate
    
    _row_field resolved ByKey('kind'/'observer'/'origin') off the row tuple, so a
    combined read gave them universal membership while SPEC §9 and the lens
    generator resolve them from the payload (non-membership when absent) — the
    same per-surface divergence as F1, one column family over.
    
    The row-shaped accessor now derives its envelope set from atoms.ENVELOPE_KEYS
    instead of restating which columns count, so it cannot drift from
    resolve_key_field. The perf property holds: the default orderings (Arrival(),
    ByKey('ts')) are envelope-only and still never reach the JSON parse.
    
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JpCUT3bF3dukDk5xjDejRM

